# R_TRIG, period 100 ms (time is irrelevant to this block).
#
# Derivation: the standard gives R_TRIG as an ST body (ed.3 table 43 /
# ed.2 table 35):
#   VAR M : BOOL; END_VAR        (* M initial value FALSE *)
#   Q := CLK AND NOT M;
#   M := CLK;
# so Q is TRUE for exactly the one evaluation in which CLK is TRUE and was
# FALSE at the previous evaluation. Because M starts FALSE, a CLK that is
# TRUE at the very first evaluation produces an edge; this trace starts with
# CLK = FALSE so that no runtime is penalised for a different initial M, and
# documents the first-call case in notes/findings.md instead.
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: clk
outputs: q
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.3.5.2 table 43 (R_TRIG body)
---
0 clk=FALSE => q=FALSE
1 clk=TRUE  => q=TRUE
2           => q=FALSE
3           => q=FALSE
4 clk=FALSE => q=FALSE
5 clk=TRUE  => q=TRUE
6 clk=FALSE => q=FALSE
7 clk=TRUE  => q=TRUE
8 clk=TRUE  => q=FALSE
